      "round_summary": "Round 3/3 — fix progress_bounded. error_type=dut_bug. root_cause: transition function Cat(posReg(4,1), ~posReg(0)) maps position 26 (binary 11010) to 27 (out of bounds); dest clamps to posReg(26) which is already visited, permanently stalling position and causing liveness timer to reach 28. Fix: (1) changed next from Cat(posReg(4,1), ~posReg(0)) to Mux(posReg===26.U, 0.U, posReg+1.U) — cyclic 0→1→2→...→25→26→0→1→... ensuring every valid position maps to another valid neighbor. (2) removed !visited(dest) guard in normal-operation when block so traversal always advances every cycle; after all 27 positions are visited the cycle continues indefinitely, keeping the liveness timer perpetually reset. Both changes are causal: (1) eliminates the out-of-bounds transition from the only sink vertex; (2) prevents post-completion stalling that would otherwise let the timer fire 28 cycles after the 27th position is visited. Target assertion label progress_bounded preserved unchanged. No homologous assertions — assertLivenessTimer appears only once in the source.",
